WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.986
Hi! We say many apples but much water. Why? Today we'll learn nouns, quantifiers, and this, that, these and those.

2
00:00:11.136 --> 00:00:15.882
Nouns we can count have plurals: apples, boxes, babies.

3
00:00:16.032 --> 00:00:22.386
Some plurals are irregular and must be learnt: children, men, feet, mice.

4
00:00:22.536 --> 00:00:27.450
Nouns we can't count have no plural: water, rice, sugar.

5
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:32.490
To count them, use a glass of, or a bowl of.

6
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.746
Countable nouns take many and a few: many books, a few pencils.

7
00:00:37.896 --> 00:00:43.386
Uncountable nouns take much and a little: much water, a little sugar.

8
00:00:43.536 --> 00:00:46.698
Some and a lot of work with both kinds.

9
00:00:46.848 --> 00:00:55.914
Near things take this and these, far things take that and those. One thing takes this or that, many take these or those.

10
00:00:56.064 --> 00:01:00.906
Watch out! Water can't be counted, so we can't use many!

11
00:01:01.056 --> 00:01:05.106
Uncountable nouns take much: not much water.

12
00:01:05.256 --> 00:01:10.746
Only countable nouns take many: not many bottles.

13
00:01:10.896 --> 00:01:20.442
Your turn! There are three, ___, in the playground. Which one? Pause and think.

14
00:01:20.592 --> 00:01:26.778
The plural of child is irregular: children. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:26.928 --> 00:01:36.570
Another one! I only have, ___, money left. Which one? Pause and think.

16
00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:42.522
Money is uncountable, so a little. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:42.672 --> 00:01:52.122
Here's another! How, ___, eggs do we need? Which one? Pause and think.

18
00:01:52.272 --> 00:01:57.690
Eggs can be counted, so many. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:07.890
Try one more! Look at, ___, birds up in the sky! Which one? Pause and think.

20
00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:14.154
Many birds, far away in the sky, so those. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:14.304 --> 00:02:24.234
Try one more! Please pass me two, ___, of bread. Which one? Pause and think.

22
00:02:24.384 --> 00:02:31.770
Bread is uncountable, so slices of bread; two needs the s. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:41.442
Last one! How, ___, water is in the bottle? Which one? Pause and think.

24
00:02:41.592 --> 00:02:47.154
Water can't be counted, so much. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:47.304 --> 00:02:58.434
Remember: first check if the noun can be counted. Countable takes many and a few, uncountable takes much and a little. Near is this and these, far is that and those.

26
00:02:58.584 --> 00:03:04.026
Look around the kitchen: what can you count, and what can't you?

